I'm trying to flash one of my NAND partition on a dev board with ubifs. 

~ # cat /proc/mtd | grep mtd5
mtd5: 15e00000 00020000 "APP"

So i want to format mtd5 with ubifs. I found mkfs parameters with:
~ # mtdinfo /dev/mtd5
mtd5
Name: APP
Type: nand
Eraseblock size: 131072 bytes, 128.0 KiB
Amount of eraseblocks: 2800 (367001600 bytes, 350.0 MiB)
Minimum input/output unit size: 2048 bytes
Sub-page size: 2048 bytes
OOB size: 64 bytes
Character device major/minor: 90:10
Bad blocks are allowed: true
Device is writable: true

The ubi.cfg file looks like:

~ # cat ubi.cfg 
[ubifs]
mode=ubi
image=ubifs.img
vol_id=0
vol_size=200MiB
vol_type=dynamic
vol_name=rootfs
vol_flags=autoresize


Well everything seems ok until i try to put it in action.

# mkfs.ubifs -m 2048 -e 129024 -c 2768 -o ubifs.img -x zlib
# ubinize -o ubi.img -m 2048 -p 128KiB -s 2048 ubi.cfg
# ubiformat /dev/mtd5 -s 2048 -f ubi.img
